This folder holds FiraGO, version 1.001, as OpenType (CFF) fonts.

FiraGO is a humanist sans by Carrois Corporate and bBox Type, built on
Fira Sans 4.3, which Erik Spiekermann and Ralph du Carrois designed for
Mozilla. Its Latin, Greek and Cyrillic are the same as Fira Sans 4.3, and
it adds Arabic, Devanagari, Georgian, Hebrew and Thai.

The family has fifteen weights, each with an italic. Eight of those thirty
styles are included here: Light, Regular, SemiBold and Bold, each with its
italic. The others are in the source repository.

The fonts were obtained from

https://github.com/bBoxType/FiraGO

(folder Fonts/FiraGO_OTF_1001) and are licensed under the SIL Open Font
License, version 1.1, with Reserved Font Name "Fira". The licence text is
in LICENSE.

FiraGO is not on CTAN, so there is no LaTeX package for it. With LuaLaTeX
or XeLaTeX, load it through fontspec by its family name, FiraGO.
